---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { GITHUB_MOD, KSP_VERSION, PRODUCT } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
	title="Get started"
	description="How to prepare for KSC Tower Network as a pilot, controller, or tower operator."
>
	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="shell">
			<h1>Get started</h1>
			<p>
				A public player ZIP and always-on community tower are still being prepared. Here is
				the honest setup path so you know what to expect when {PRODUCT} goes live.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2>Requirements</h2>
			</div>
			<ul class="checklist" style="max-width: 42rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
				<li>Kerbal Space Program {KSP_VERSION} (Windows x64 for the bundled voice bridge).</li>
				<li>Module Manager (required dependency).</li>
				<li>A tower API URL from your community operator — or host your own.</li>
				<li>Recommended: ClickThroughBlocker so tower panels do not click through to the craft.</li>
			</ul>

			<div class="prose">
				<h2>If you want to fly</h2>
				<p>
					When the release pack ships, you drop <code>GameData/KSCTowerNetwork/</code> into
					your KSP install, launch the game, and connect with the baked-in tower host.
					Until that ZIP is published, follow the open repository and wait for a tagged
					release.
				</p>
				<div class="cta-row" style="margin: 1.25rem 0 2.5rem;">
					<a class="btn btn-primary" href={GITHUB_MOD} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
						>View mod on GitHub</a
					>
					<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">Read the loop</a>
				</div>

				<h2>If you want to control</h2>
				<p>
					Controllers only need a browser and credentials for a hosted tower desk. No KSP
					install required. When a public session is announced, you will open the tower URL,
					sign in, and take the seat.
				</p>

				<h2>If you want to host</h2>
				<p>
					Operators stand up the API, web desk, and LiveKit project, then run the packaging
					script so player builds point at those hosts. The mod repo documents env vars,
					CORS, MariaDB, Redis, and the release ZIP flow.
				</p>
				<p>
					Status right now: the product stack exists and is documented for production; this
					site is the public front door. The playable hosted tower endpoint is still being
					brought online.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
